BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Calligraphy Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
UID:introduction-to-calligraphy-workshop-2026-10-24t13-00-00-04-00@agakhan
 museum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Elevated_Calligraphy_Workshop_Shirin_Divanbeigi2-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600
 -1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Explore the timeless art of calligraphy in this hands-on works
 hop\, where our Museum Educators guide you through the graceful strokes\, 
 expressive forms\, and creative possibilities behind this centuries-old pr
 actice.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-calligraphy-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Water Marbling Bookmarks Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
UID:water-marbling-bookmarks-workshop-2026-10-24t15-00-00-04-00@agakhanmus
 eum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Water-Marbling-Workshop_Bookmarks_MadalinaRaduta1-scaled-aspect-ratio-160
 0-1000-scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Immerse yourself in the mesmerizing world of water marbling 
 — an ancient technique of floating pigments on water and transferring th
 em onto paper to create intricate\, fluid designs.\n\nPracticed for centur
 ies across the Islamic world\, particularly in regions such as Türkiye\, 
 Iran\, and the Indian subcontinent\, water marbling has been used to adorn
  calligraphy\, manuscripts\, and decorative papers. In this introductory w
 orkshop\, you will explore its rich history and cultural significance whil
 e mastering traditional tools and methods to produce a variety of classic 
 patterns. Guided step-by-step\, you will create between five and eight uni
 que marbled bookmarks to take home — each a one-of-a-kind reflection of 
 colour\, movement\, and your own creative expression.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-water-marbling-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pt. Partho Sarothy\, Vidushi Mita Nag\, and Pt. Subhen Chatterjee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T193000
UID:pt-partho-sarothy-vidushi-mita-nag-and-pt-subhen-chatterjee-2026-10-24
 t19-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/10
 /Website-design-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Bringing together three distinguished artists of Hindustani cl
 assical music\, this performance unites the expressive sounds of the sarod
 \, sitar\, and tabla. Sarod maestro Pt. Partho Sarothy \, acclaimed sitari
 st Vidushi Mita Nag \, and tabla virtuoso Pt. Subhen Chatterjee come toget
 her for an evening of intricate melody\, rhythmic interplay\, and spontane
 ous musical exchange.\n\nDrawing on generations of musical lineage and dec
 ades of performance experience\, the artists bring distinct approaches and
  traditions to the stage. From the resonant depth of the sarod and the lyr
 ical beauty of the sitar to the intricate rhythms of the tabla\, the perfo
 rmance celebrates the artistry\, improvisation\, and enduring legacy of In
 dian classical music.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/partho-vidushi-subhen/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2026-10-24t13-00-00-04-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/10
 /Mosaic-Coaster_PaidWorkshop_MadalinaRaduta6-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000
 -scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-fasayfisa-mosaic-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T130000
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2026-10-25t13-00-00-04-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/10
 /Mosaic-Coaster_PaidWorkshop_MadalinaRaduta6-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000
 -scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-fasayfisa-mosaic-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Colour Impressions: Exploring Gelli Plate Monoprinting Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T150000
UID:colour-impressions-exploring-gelli-plate-monoprinting-workshop-2026-10
 -25t15-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /MicrosoftTeams-image-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravit
 y
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the Museum’s collections\, this hands-on worksho
 p explores the foundational elements of Islamic art\, from geometry and pr
 oportion to rhythm and ornament\, with a particular focus on geometric and
  floral motifs.\n\nThrough guided exploration and mindful experimentation 
 with Gel plate monoprinting\, participants will learn techniques such as l
 ayering\, masking\, and texture transfer to create original prints. This r
 elaxed\, process-oriented workshop invites reflection on the interplay bet
 ween colour\, form\, and pattern\, resulting in vibrant\, one-of-a-kind wo
 rks inspired by the timeless beauty of our collections.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-gelli-plate-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
