BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Labyrinth Ensemble with Canan Sezgin Geylan and Yahya Geylan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T200000
UID:labyrinth-ensemble-with-canan-sezgin-geylan-and-yahya-geylan-2026-11-0
 7t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/10
 /20260509-409-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&g
 ravity
DESCRIPTION:The thirteen member Ensemble is thrilled to be back in the Nan
 ji Family Foundation Auditorium to present this captivating and heartfelt 
 performance.\n\nThere is nothing in the world of modal music quite like th
 e Labyrinth Ensemble. A fiercely eclectic group — think Hardanger fiddle
 \, guzheng and microtonal guitar — they drink deeply from tradition to c
 reate unique\, contemporary concert experiences.\n\nToronto’s premier la
 rge modal music group returns to the Aga Khan Museum for an evening of cla
 ssical Turkish repertoire. Husband-wife duo Canan Sezgin Geylan and Yahya 
 Geylan will lead the Labyrinth Ensemble through two weeks of intensive stu
 dy and rehearsal\, teaching them the rich vocabulary of Turkish modal musi
 c.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/labyrinth-ensemble-with-geylan/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chai & Jam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T200000
UID:chai-jam-2026-11-14t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /ChaiJam_Promo_2-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Chai & Jam brings together Indian Classical\, Jazz\, R&B\, and
  World musicians together for a one-of-a-kind improvised performance. Havi
 ng completed 5 sold out seasons\, the show features spontaneous collaborat
 ions\, and post-show conversations about the music and improvisation behin
 d the performance.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/chai-and-jam/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Duende International Flamenco Festival: Masterclasses
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
UID:2026-duende-international-flamenco-festival-masterclasses-2026-11-18@a
 gakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /25.11_AK_Duende_3__5167-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1
 584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:This special series of masterclasses offers dancers a rare opp
 ortunity to learn with three extraordinary flamenco artists\, Óscar de lo
 s Reyes\, Carmen Talegona\, and El Yiyo.\n\nEach workshop offers participa
 nts a deeper understanding of the art form’s power\, precision\, musical
 ity\, and emotional truth. The three artists brings a distinct voice\, lin
 eage\, and approach\, guiding dancers toward greater technical clarity\, e
 xpressive range\, and connection to rhythm\, structure\, and cante. Togeth
 er\, these masterclasses create a rich encounter with flamenco as a living
 \, evolving art form — one that honours tradition while continuing to mo
 ve boldly into the future.\n\nOpen to intermediate\, advanced\, and profes
 sional-level dancers\, the workshops offer an inspiring environment for gr
 owth\, exchange\, and artistic discovery.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-duende-international-flamenco-
 festival-masterclasses/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Farruquito: A Flamenco Dynasty
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
UID:farruquito-a-flamenco-dynasty-2026-11-18t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.
 org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /01_FARRUQUITO-A-FLAMENCO-DYNASTY_CAPA-ESPANA-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?r
 esize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Aga Khan Museum’s 12th annual Duende Internation
 al Flamenco Festival: Flamenco and the World\, join us for a film screenin
 g that celebrates the legacy of Farruquito\, one of the greatest flamenco 
 dancers of this century.\n\nFarruquito is celebrated as the finest flamenc
 o dancer of his generation. He belongs to a legendary dynasty of bailaores
  (dancers). At only 20\, he was already at the height of his success\, cap
 tivating audiences around the globe from New York to Tokyo – with his ex
 traordinary talent\, yet the shadows of his family’s tumultuous history 
 loomed large.\n\nThe film follows Farruquito’s journey through triumph a
 nd tragedy\, focusing on a pivotal moment that changes everything — a tr
 agic accident that leads to the death of a pedestrian and lands him in pri
 son. This harrowing experience forces him to confront the demons of his pa
 st and the heavy burden of his family’s legacy.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/farruquito-a-flamenco-dynasty/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Duende International Flamenco Festival: Flamenco and the World
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
UID:duende-international-flamenco-festival-flamenco-and-the-world-2026-11-
 18@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /25.11_AK_Duende_5__3164-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1
 584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate flamenco’s global transformation through cross-cul
 tural exchange at the Aga Khan Museum’s 12th annual Duende International
  Flamenco Festival: Flamenco and the World.\n\nFrom November 18 to 22\, ex
 perience the vibrant evolution of flamenco — from its regional roots in 
 Andalusia to a dynamic global art form shaped by cross-cultural exchange. 
 This year’s lineup spans both traditional flamenco from Andalusia and in
 novative collaborations at the crossroads of qawwali and Persian muqam\, t
 racing the art form’s evolution from its regional roots to a global prac
 tice.\n\nThursday\, November 19 • 8 pm
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, Massey Hall\, Nanji Family Foundation Auditoriu
 m
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/duende-2026/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qawwali Flamenco
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:qawwali-flamenco-2026-11-19t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Qawwali_FlamencoFestival-de-Saint-Denis-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-sca
 led.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:From Pakistan to Andalusia\, musical traditions have crossed p
 aths\, met\, nourished one another\, and blended so thoroughly that betwee
 n the volcanic power and virtuosity of qawwali singing and the hypnotic ly
 ricism of flamenco\, distances fade and similarities naturally emerge.\n\n
 Qawwali Flamenco marks the long-awaited return of the celebrated collabora
 tion between Pakistani qawwali master Faiz Ali Faiz and flamenco guitar vi
 rtuoso Juan Gómez “Chicuelo.”\n\nFollowing their acclaimed first coll
 aboration a decade ago\, Faiz and Gómez reunite to deepen a remarkable ar
 tistic dialogue. The first chapter of their Qawwali Flamenco journey explo
 red the relationship between human beings and their beloved\; this new cre
 ation turns toward the connection between humanity and the divine.
LOCATION:Massey Hall\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M
 3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/qawwali-flamenco/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blackbird: In the Footsteps of Ziryab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T200000
UID:blackbird-in-the-footsteps-of-ziryab-2026-11-20t20-00-00-05-00@agakhan
 museum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Oscar-de-los-Reyes-upper-body-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?re
 size=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Blackbird: In the Footsteps of Ziryab makes its world premiere
  as a bold new multidisciplinary performance celebrating the enduring conn
 ections between cultures through oral and artistic traditions. Led by Arti
 stic Director Amir Amiri\, the Amir Amiri Ensemble\, featuring Óscar de l
 os Reyes and Esperanza Soria\, the performance brings together Canadian an
 d Spanish Andalusian artists in a powerful artistic dialogue. Connected th
 rough centuries of migration\, poetry\, rhythm\, and memory\, the performa
 nce explores a shared cultural legacy while embracing new creative express
 ion. The essentials of flamenco are all present: voice\, complex rhythm\, 
 and dance.\n\nThis presentation ultimately asks how music travels through 
 history\, how cultures reshape one another\, and how artists continue to c
 arry ancient knowledge into contemporary life. The project seeks to illumi
 nate the enduring connections between Persian and Andalusian artistic worl
 ds\, while creating a contemporary performance grounded in research\, arti
 stic integrity\, and shared humanity.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/blackbird/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flamenco: Made in Canada presents Duende Al Nur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T200000
UID:flamenco-made-in-canada-presents-duende-al-nur-2026-11-21t20-00-00-05-
 00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Webpage-Image-Nan-Carmen-shawl-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C9
 90&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Duende al Nur \, meaning “Duende toward the light\,” is an
  immersive flamenco work where light\, shadow and fire transform the danci
 ng body.\n\nPerformed on a luminous plexiglass platform\, the piece explor
 es light as a sacred\, living force rising from beneath the dancer. From d
 arkness\, the body is awakened by illumination. Breath becomes pulse\, pul
 se becomes rhythm\, and rhythm becomes flamenco. Through footwork\, castan
 ets\, zills\, breath and silence\, Carmen Romero moves through a ritual jo
 urney of awakening and renewal. Rooted in the emotional power of duende an
 d the Arabic resonance of nur\, the work becomes a passage through memory\
 , prayer\, rhythm and transformation.\n\nThe work draws from flamenco’s 
 emotional intensity\, rhythmic complexity and theatrical power while openi
 ng the performance space to Arabic resonance\, sacred illumination and imm
 ersive sound. Rather than presenting cultural influence literally\, Duende
  al Nur approaches these elements as echoes\, atmospheres and poetic point
 s of connection.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/duende-flamenco-made-in-canada/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Los Magníficos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T200000
UID:los-magn-ficos-2026-11-22t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /LosMagnificos_Varios1_NoeliaVela-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg
 ?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:“Los Magníficos” is a once-in-a-lifetime encounter with t
 he greatness of contemporary flamenco. Five outstanding artists come toget
 her in a unique performance where singing\, dance\, guitar\, and piano rea
 ch their highest expression.\n\nSandra Carrasco\, one of the most importan
 t voices of the moment\, takes us to the very heart of flamenco. David de 
 Arahal captivates audiences with his mastery of the guitar\, while Andrés
  Barrios transforms the piano into pure emotion. Dancer “El Yiyo” embo
 dies the power and intensity of flamenco\, joined by Carmen “La Talegona
 \,” whose artistry and magnetic stage presence bring elegance\, strength
 \, and depth to this extraordinary encounter.\n\nPrepare for an intense an
 d magnetic journey\, where energy and sensitivity intertwine in an explosi
 on of talent. “ Los Magníficos” is not just a performance\; it’s a 
 unique opportunity to witness the union of some of the finest artists of o
 ur time in a moment destined to remain forever in the memory of flamenco a
 rt.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/los-magnificos/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
